From 3dcd1f68ab18de35177ff03c981c97706191196f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:34:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the solvers and preconditioners of hypre not wrapped by
 MFEM

The BiCGSTAB, COGMRES and LGMRES Krylov solvers of hypre, its hybrid
solver (diagonal scaling, then BoomerAMG when the convergence is slow)
and its factorized sparse approximate inverse are implemented in
src/HypreSolvers.{hxx,cxx}, after mfem::HypreGMRES:

- the convergence of the Krylov solvers is given by the indicator of
  hypre and by the code returned by the resolution (a breakdown of
  BiCGSTAB is not a convergence, a null right hand side is one);
- the dimension of the Krylov space is 50 by default, as for HypreGMRES;
- the hybrid solver logs its final residual (otherwise hypre does not
  compute it), and is built again for each operator and each change of
  its tolerance (its inner solver keeps the first tolerance);
- the factorized approximate inverse is built again for each operator.

In src/HypreLinearSolvers.cxx:

- one generator for all the Krylov solvers of hypre; COGMRES only
  computes on the host and is refused when hypre computes on a GPU; the
  Krylov solvers of hypre refuse the preconditioners applied by MFEM;
- the options of BoomerAMG are given by a table, with the ranges of
  hypre (TruncationFactor, MaximumElementsPerRow,
  AggressiveInterpolationType, NumberOfPaths, MaximumCoarseSize,
  MinimumCoarseSize, RelaxationWeight, ChebyshevOrder and KeepTranspose
  are new; StrengthThreshold is checked in [0, 1]);
- the HypreSmoother preconditioner gives the smoothers of hypre applied
  by MFEM (Jacobi, l1-Jacobi, Gauss-Seidel, polynomial smoothers); the
  OPFS, Taubin, FIR and lumped Jacobi smoothers only compute on the host
  and are refused when hypre computes on a GPU;
- the HypreFSAI preconditioner and the HypreHybrid solver.
